                        "review": "Pros: \n- Multiple game modes (CTF, King of the Hill, Battle Royale, Dungeon).\n- Customizable ship.\n- Good graphics and gameplay.\n\nCons:\n- Co-Op levels require a certain minimum amount of players. Cannot add AI to replace them, thus cannot play the levels (on top of a level requirement).\n- Level requirements makes this into more of a grind to unlock the next level.\n- Because of the player count requirements, you'll mostly be grinding just 1 level that will be available to you.\n- Ridiculously overpriced DLCs.\n\nThoughts and Notes / Recommendation for Devs: \n- The game has incredible potential, and I hope it will one day breathe with life, as current population is low, which is only further contributed by the locked levels with both a player and level requirement.\n- Remove the locks on the levels, allow AI to replace players (or remove the minimum requirement if AI is impossible), and allow the AI to be replaced in a game session by a newly joined player (to prevent lobby waiting).\n- Definitely add more maps, perhaps with a mini-story to have players engaged. The way things are now, I think \"Dungeon\" with no requirements should be prioritized for development, as it will increase the chances of players willing to keep the game in their inventory (as of now, most players only have the option to play and re-play the only single-player dungeon map). Especially if I need to pay $100 USD to unlock all content, I'd like more content..\n\nSentence:\nVery chill, laidback and relaxing, good looking atmospheric classical styled casual top-down space defender shooter.",
